& [PostIR6ImplementationReadinessSurfaceV1] is the current implementation-readiness surface after IR6 implementation acceptance
  + [surface_state] is ready_for_IR7_final_slice_minting
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is IR6CoordinationMailboxProjectionImplementationProofPack
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is IR6ImplementationCompletionReview
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is FSC5OperationsSafetyPackV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is PostFSC5ImplementationReadinessSurfaceV1
  + [active_implementation_chunk] is IR7 operations dry-run request simulator planning
  + [gated_chunk] is IR7 implementation activation until IR7 final planning is accepted
  + [gated_chunk] is live-control authority reconsideration until separate source-preserved SJS authority is accepted
  + [safety_limit] is no live operations control authorized

  = must: mint IR7 final slices before writing operations simulator code, fixture files, expected ledgers, generated outputs, dependencies, adapters, transports, or package metadata
  = must: run completion review after each IR7 planning slice before opening downstream slices
  = must: preserve IR6 coordination proof boundaries for claims, mailbox carriers, human overrides, conflict review, completion gates, and no mailbox IO
  = must: preserve FSC5 operations dry-run-only and live-control prohibition boundaries
  = must: keep operations dry-run-only unless a separate future live-control authority is source-preserved, SJS-processed, least-privilege bounded, and accepted

& [ImplementationReadinessChunk: IR7OperationsDryRunRequestSimulatorPlanning] is ready_for_slice_minting
  + [chunk_id] is IR7
  + [chunk_name] is operations dry-run request simulator planning
  + [boundary_input_set] is docs/planning/IR6_Coordination_Mailbox_Projection_Prototype_Implementation_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
  + [boundary_input_set] is docs/reviews/IR6_Implementation_Completion_Review.v1.sop
  + [boundary_input_set] is docs/planning/FSC5_Operations_Safety_Pack.v1.sop
  + [boundary_input_set] is docs/canonical/LangSOP_Operations_Safety_Spec.canonical.sop
  + [expected_output_set] is IR7 final slice surface
  + [expected_output_set] is operation request simulator boundary import
  + [expected_output_set] is dry-run request, result, refusal, and safety classification contracts
  + [expected_output_set] is operations dry-run fixture plan and fixture index
  + [expected_output_set] is implementation activation pack for future dry-run simulator work
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [model_route_reason] is operations manager, job-control simulation, resource-boundary modeling, future dispatch, and live-control safety semantics require new authority review
  + [future_bounded_fixture_route] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable only after IR7 final planning accepts fixture boundaries
  + [forbidden_scope] is operations simulator implementation, command execution, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, job dispatch, credential access or mutation, network exposure mutation, destructive filesystem action, persistent operations automation, operations control, and live machine control

  = must: split IR7 into final planning slices before implementation activation
  = must: preserve dry-run-only semantics and refuse live effects as records

& [IR7FinalSliceCandidateSet] is the recommended first final-slice minting shape for IR7
  + [slice_candidate] is IR7-S01 boundary import and invariant reconciliation
  + [slice_candidate] is IR7-S02 dry-run operation request and result contract
  + [slice_candidate] is IR7-S03 resource safety, human approval, and refusal projection contract
  + [slice_candidate] is IR7-S04 operations dry-run fixture plan and fixture index
  + [slice_candidate] is IR7-S05 implementation plan and activation pack
  + [slice_candidate] is IR7-S06 final planning completion review

  = must: keep IR7-S01, IR7-S02, IR7-S03, IR7-S05, and IR7-S06 under deeper reasoning
  = should: route bounded IR7-S04 fixture drafting to GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark only after IR7-S01 through IR7-S03 are accepted
  = must: keep all slices non-mutating and non-live

& [IR7ReadinessSafetyBoundary] is the safety boundary for the opened IR7 planning chunk
  + [dry_run_request_record_authorized] is true_for_planning_only
  + [dry_run_result_schema_authorized] is true_for_planning_only
  + [refusal_record_schema_authorized] is true_for_planning_only
  + [human_approval_record_schema_authorized] is true_for_planning_only
  + [operations_simulator_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [fixture_file_creation_authorized] is false_until_IR7_final_slice_opens_it
  + [expected_ledger_creation_authorized] is false_until_IR7_final_slice_opens_it
  + [generated_output_creation_authorized] is false_until_future_implementation_activation
  + [dependency_installation_authorized] is false
  + [package_metadata_mutation_authorized] is false
  + [agent_dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [operations_control_authorized] is false
  + [live_machine_control_authorized] is false

  = must: treat operation-like requests as records for review, dry-run, refusal, or future authorization, not as commands
  = must: reject dry-run success, fixture success, projected user intent, broad approval, mailbox notice, or carrier state as live-control authority
  = must: require separate future live-control authority before any live process, GPU, model runtime, job, credential, network, destructive filesystem, persistent automation, or machine-control effect

& [PostIR6ReadinessClosureReview] is the dependency audit for the post-IR6 implementation surface
  + [IR6_implementation_proof_status] is accepted
  + [IR6_implementation_completion_status] is accepted
  + [FSC5_operations_safety_status] is accepted
  + [post_FSC5_readiness_lineage_status] is accepted
  + [current_ready_chunk_set] is IR7
  + [unresolved_external_dependency_set] is empty_after_gate
  + [forbidden_external_dependency_found] is false
  + [operations_simulator_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [agent_dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [operations_control_authorized] is false
  + [live_machine_control_authorized] is false

  = must: treat implementation activation, live-control authority, and downstream operations execution as gated, not ready
  = must: rerun closure review when a boundary pack changes, proof fails, or implementation contradiction appears
